  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One Day. One Focus:  Ending   Polio 24 October</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Polio used to be common in the United States. Before the polio vaccine, the disease killed thousands of people and paralyzed about 15,000 each year. Thanks to the polio vaccine, we&apos;ve come close to ending polio, but it continues to threaten communities in parts of the globe. In rural communities, infants, babies have commonly suffer innocently in this danger.  Getting vaccinated is the best way to prevent polio.</narrative>
  </description>
